<article class="env-lemma" id="0EWY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EWY">Lemma <span data-tag="0EWY">15.15.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Suppose that $\varphi : R^ n \to R^ n$ be an injective map of finite free modules of the same rank. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(\varphi ), R) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\varphi ^ t : R^ n \to R^ n$ be the transpose of $\varphi $. The lemma claims that $\varphi ^ t$ is injective. With notation as in Lemma <a href="/tag/00MX" data-tag="00MX">15.15.6</a> we see that the rank of $\varphi ^ t$ is $n$ and that $I(\varphi ) = I(\varphi ^ t)$. Thus we conclude by the equivalence of (1) and (2) of the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>